# Intel E810 OS-Default DDP package

`ice.pkg` is Intel's OS-Default Dynamic Device Personalization package,
version 1.3.41.0.  The ice(4D) driver loads it during attach through
`firmware_open(9F)`.  If it is absent or rejected, the driver deliberately
falls back to Safe Mode.

`usr/src/uts/intel/ice/Makefile` installs the package as
`/kernel/firmware/ice/ice.pkg`.  The package manifest must include that path
when the driver is integrated into an IPS package.  A successful attach logs
the active package name and version reported by the device to the system log.

The file is imported byte-for-byte from FreeBSD `freebsd-src` commit
`d0b1a389003b1e6ff5bcf35a7c04654ea7ff87bd`:

```
sys/contrib/dev/ice/ice-1.3.41.0.pkg
```

FreeBSD identifies the package as version 1.3.41.0 in
`sys/modules/ice_ddp/Makefile`.  The imported FreeBSD Git blob is
`71e75a5d78365ae4a23bef57776e835e5009bc29`.

The SHA-256 digest of `ice.pkg` is:

```
2925f8601490d4341dec36e27aa08e17c419ba2d9b4c7c0c6e798b2fe14cff92
```

Do not modify the package.  Updates must come from a redistributable Intel or
FreeBSD release and must update the provenance, digest, and accompanying
license in the same change.
